      notes: """
        Looking at this place-time plot can help us analyze existing debugging tools and envision new ones.

        We can see the ways in which breakpoints and print statements are limited, locked to particular slices of place and time.

        We can look at the Whyline, a set of papers by Amy Ko, which provides "why did this happen" style analyses of program states. These look like links between points in place-time. Whyline lets you query in a way that crosses place and time simultaneously in a semantically meaningful way.
      """
    }
